### npm package: MCP server, CLI, and SDK

The [@speedofme/mcp](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@speedofme/mcp) package (Node.js 18+) runs accurate speed tests three ways from a single install: `npx -y @speedofme/mcp` or `npm i -g @speedofme/mcp`.

- [Package on npm](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@speedofme/mcp): Install, CLI, SDK, and MCP usage
- [GitHub MCP Registry listing](https://github.com/mcp/me.speedof/speed-test): Official entry, with one-line install for Claude Code and a standard MCP client config
- [MCP integration docs](https://speedof.me/api/docs/#mcp-integrations): Client configs and agent-framework examples

**MCP server** (for AI agents): exposes `run_speed_test` and `get_test_history` tools, plus `speedofme://history` and `speedofme://config` resources. Works with Claude Code, Claude Desktop, Cursor, Windsurf, Zed, VS Code (Copilot), Cline, Continue, JetBrains, and Goose, and with agent frameworks such as LangChain, LlamaIndex, AutoGen, CrewAI, and Semantic Kernel.

**CLI** (for scripts and terminals): `npx -y @speedofme/mcp --progress` runs a test, `--json` emits machine-readable output for automation, and `history` lists past results.

**SDK** (for Node.js apps): a promise-based `SpeedTest` class returns structured results (download, upload, latency, jitter, plus test server and timestamp). Configure `sustainTime`, the specific `tests` to run, gigabit mode, and local history.

### In-browser WebMCP tools (no install)

The homepages (`/` and `/m/`) expose WebMCP tools directly to AI agents running inside a WebMCP-capable browser (via `document.modelContext`). No account or install is needed: an in-browser agent can run a test, share the result, and read past results. The tools are registered at runtime, so the same list is also published as a static file at [/.well-known/webmcp](https://speedof.me/.well-known/webmcp) for anything that does not execute page JavaScript.

- `run_speed_test`: run a single on-page speed test; returns download/upload (Mbps), latency, jitter, and the test server
- `create_share_link`: publish the latest result as a public i.speedof.me share link
- `get_past_results`: read this browser's saved test history with all-time averages
- `get_developer_api`: links to the developer API/SDK/CLI/MCP for automated or at-scale testing

These run a single free test per call inside the browser. For repeated, scheduled, headless, or at-scale testing, use the @speedofme/mcp package or the JavaScript API instead.

### Machine-readable discovery

Three static files describe everything on this domain an agent can call, with no page rendering required:

- [/.well-known/ai-catalog.json](https://speedof.me/.well-known/ai-catalog.json): ARD capability manifest listing both the MCP server and the in-browser WebMCP tools. Also linked from `robots.txt` (`Agentmap:`) and from a `<link rel="ai-catalog">` tag on the homepages
- [/.well-known/mcp.json](https://speedof.me/.well-known/mcp.json): server card for the @speedofme/mcp package (name, version, install, required environment)
- [/.well-known/webmcp](https://speedof.me/.well-known/webmcp): the four in-browser WebMCP tools with their input schemas

All three are generated from the same source as the running code, so they cannot drift from the tools actually served.

